questions.explanation:
This question tests end-to-end thinking for a real-time AWS ML workflow with PrivateLink, including model choice, training strategy, endpoint sizing, canary rollout, and monitoring for drift and privacy. Key concepts covered include SageMaker training with transfer learning on image-caption data, PrivateLink access to a VPC-hosted endpoint, real-time endpoint autoscaling and latency targeting, canary rollout and rollback criteria, and Model Monitor for drift and privacy checks.

```javascript
// Training config
const config = {
  encoder: 'EfficientNet-Lite0',
  decoder: 'TransformerDecoder',
  vocabularySize: 8000,
  augmentation: ['random_crop', 'horizontal_flip', 'color_jitter'],
  learningRate: 0.001,
  batchSize: 32,
  epochs: 20
};

// Endpoint config
const endpointConfig = {
  instanceType: 'ml.g4dn.xlarge',
  minInstances: 1,
  maxInstances: 3,
  scalingTarget: { metric: 'P99Latency', value: 500 },
  cooldown: 300
};

// Canary rollout
const canaryConfig = {
  initialTraffic: 5,
  stages: [5, 25, 50, 100],
  stageDuration: 86400,
  rollback: { latencyThreshold: 600, errorRateThreshold: 0.01 }
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of SageMaker for anomaly detection, focusing on real-time latency requirements, data residency constraints, and phased deployment strategies using canary releases.

## Key Concepts
- Anomaly detection models (Isolation Forest, autoencoders)
- Time-series feature engineering (rolling windows)
- Endpoint configuration and autoscaling (min/max instances, latency targets)
- Monitoring and drift detection (SageMaker Clarify, CloudWatch)
- Cost optimization and regional data compliance

